Shoals.Dupire.du_cubic_log_moneyness_interp: strikes must be strictly increasing: index 2 has strike 90.0, which does not exceed strike 90.0 at index 1

Strict ordering on the strike axis too. Two knots at one strike carry two
different implied vols for one option, so no smile reads both, and the segment
width between them is zero -- which `spline_fit` does not reject: at a zero
gap every leg of its tridiagonal fit substitutes 1.0, and it solves a system
whose geometry no longer matches the knots it was given. (The legs do not all
agree for a *negative* gap, which is a separate Nautilus question and not what
this fixture exercises.) This is the negative-parity case for
the `gt` in the strike guard; a `gte` would accept it and the reordered strike
case would still be rejected.

The unguarded query at k=95 returned 0.25239202. There is no "correct" value
to compare that against, because the fixture asks what the implied vol is at a
strike the grid gives two different answers for; the defect is that the call
answers at all.
